[1m[38;5;231mHow should the user's identity be recorded?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mPseudonymous ID (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mStable hash of the username. Distinct-user counts and funnels still work; records are not directly identifying. [39m
     [38;5;246mCheap now, costly to retrofit.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Raw username
     [38;5;246mStore the login name as-is. Simplest and best for debugging, but makes every stored record personal data.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m No identity at all
     [38;5;246mRecord only that a login occurred and whether it succeeded. Answers how many, not who.[39m
